.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt PROTON-FIRESAFE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm proton-firesafe
.Nd keep Proton Drive takeouts on two rotating, encrypted disks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm run
.Nm
.Cm takeout
.Nm
.Cm eject
.Nm
.Cm status
.Nm
.Cm init
.Ar volume
.Nm
.Cm test-mail
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
keeps an offline copy of a Proton Drive account on whichever of two
external disks is attached to a Mac, and sends email when it is time to
swap that disk for the one in the fire safe.
.Pp
It is meant to run once a day, from a
.Xr launchd 8
agent.
Each run looks for an attached disk, makes a fresh takeout on it with
.Ql proton-drive takeout run
if the newest one is a week old, and keeps the two newest.
Once a disk has been attached for four weeks,
.Nm
makes one more takeout, ejects the disk, and asks by email for it to be
put in the fire safe and the other one plugged in.
At any time, one disk holds a takeout from the last week, and the other,
in the fire safe, one from the last month or so.
.Pp
The disks must be APFS (Encrypted) volumes, named as in
.Ev DISKS ,
and set up with
.Cm init .
.Nm
refuses to write a takeout to an unencrypted volume.
A disk's password needs to be saved in the login keychain so that it
mounts by itself when plugged in; see
.Sx EXAMPLES .
.Pp
A takeout is written to
.Pa takeout- Ns Ar YYYYmmdd-HHMMSS Ns Pa .partial
on the disk, and renamed without the
.Pa .partial
once
.Xr proton-drive 1
has written its
.Pa manifest.json ,
which it does once every section has finished.
If some items cannot be exported,
.Xr proton-drive 1
still writes the manifest but exits with an error; such a takeout is kept
and counted, and reported by email, so that one file that will not
download does not hold up every takeout and swap.
.Pp
Before a takeout,
.Nm
deletes older takeouts if the disk might not have room for one the size
of the newest, but never deletes the newest.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm run
Do whatever is due: ask for a disk if none is attached, make a takeout,
eject the disk and ask for a swap, or send a reminder.
This is the default, and what the
.Xr launchd 8
agent runs.
It exits 0 unless something is wrong with the configuration; failures
are reported by email instead.
.It Cm takeout
Make a takeout on the attached disk now, whether or not one is due.
.It Cm eject
Eject the attached disk, as for a swap, so that it can be swapped early.
.It Cm status
Show which disk is attached, whether it is encrypted, how much room it
has, when the next takeout and swap are due, the takeouts on it, and the
newest takeout on each disk.
.It Cm init Ar volume
Set up a mounted volume to receive takeouts, by creating the
.Pa .proton-firesafe
marker file on it.
The volume must be encrypted, and named in
.Ev DISKS .
.It Cm test-mail
Send a test message to
.Ev MAILTO .
.It Cm version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
reads the
.Xr sh 1
file
.Pa ~/.config/proton-firesafe/config ,
if it exists, which can set any of the following.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev MAILTO
Where to send email.
Without it, nothing is sent; what would have been is logged.
.It Ev MAILFROM
The
.Ql "From:"
of the email.
The default is
.Ql proton-firesafe on Ar host Aq Ev MAILTO .
.It Ev SENDMAIL
The command that sends a message, which it reads, headers and all, from
its standard input.
The default is
.Ql /opt/local/bin/msmtp -t .
.It Ev PROTON_DRIVE
The
.Xr proton-drive 1
command.
The default is
.Pa /opt/local/bin/proton-drive .
.It Ev DISKS
The volume names of the disks, separated by spaces.
The default is
.Ql Firesafe-A Firesafe-B .
More than two can be named.
.It Ev SECTIONS
The takeout sections to include, separated by spaces: any of
.Cm my-files ,
.Cm devices ,
.Cm photos ,
and
.Cm revisions ,
which also needs
.Cm my-files
or
.Cm devices .
The default is
.Ql my-files devices photos .
.It Ev TAKEOUT_EVERY_DAYS
How often to make a takeout.
The default is 7.
.It Ev SWAP_AFTER_DAYS
How long a disk stays attached before a swap.
The default is 28.
.It Ev KEEP_TAKEOUTS
How many takeouts to keep on each disk.
The default is 2.
.It Ev REMIND_EVERY_DAYS
How often to repeat a reminder about something that needs doing, such as
plugging in a disk.
The default is 7.
.It Ev TAKEOUT_WARN_HOURS
How long a takeout can run before
.Nm
sends email to say that it is still going, or 0 for never.
The default is 24.
.It Ev STATUS_EVERY_DAYS
How often to send a report that all is well, or 0 for never.
The default is 0, since the swap requests come often enough to show that
.Nm
is still running.
.It Ev ALLOW_UNENCRYPTED
Set to
.Ql yes
to allow takeouts to unencrypted volumes.
Do not.
.El
.Sh EMAIL
.Nm
sends these messages, each with a subject starting
.Ql [proton-firesafe] .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It no backup disk attached
No set-up disk is mounted.
Repeated every
.Ev REMIND_EVERY_DAYS ,
counting from the swap request.
If a disk seems to be attached but locked, or mounted but not set up,
the message says so.
.It Ar disk No is in place
The first takeout on a newly attached disk has finished.
.It time to swap the backup disks
The attached disk has had its last takeout and been ejected.
.It Ar disk No should be in the fire safe
The disk that was just swapped out has been plugged back in.
Takeouts carry on to it, and the message is repeated every
.Ev REMIND_EVERY_DAYS ,
until another disk is attached.
.It takeout to Ar disk No failed
Repeated daily until a takeout works.
.It takeout to Ar disk No is taking a long time
A takeout has been running for
.Ev TAKEOUT_WARN_HOURS .
It may just be big, or it may be stuck; while it runs,
.Xr launchd 8
starts no other run, so nothing else would say so.
.It takeout to Ar disk No finished with Ar n No failed item(s)
.It Ar disk No is too full for a new takeout
.It Ar disk No is not encrypted
.It could not eject Ar disk
.It status: Ar disk No attached
Only if
.Ev STATUS_EVERY_DAYS
is set.
.El
.Pp
None of them name files: the output of
.Xr proton-drive 1 ,
which does, is kept on the encrypted disk instead.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/proton-firesafe/config
Configuration.
.It Pa ~/Library/Application Support/proton-firesafe/
State: which disk is attached and since when, the newest takeout on each
disk, and when each reminder was last sent.
.It Pa ~/Library/Logs/proton-firesafe.log
What happened, without file names.
.It Pa ~/Library/LaunchAgents/nl.strandkip.proton-firesafe.plist
The
.Xr launchd 8
agent that runs
.Nm
daily.
.El
.Pp
On each disk:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa .proton-firesafe
Marks the volume as set up.
.It Pa .last-takeout
When its newest takeout was started, in seconds since the epoch.
.It Pa takeout- Ns Ar YYYYmmdd-HHMMSS Ns Pa /
A takeout, as written by
.Xr proton-drive 1 .
.It Pa takeout- Ns Ar YYYYmmdd-HHMMSS Ns Pa .log
The output of
.Xr proton-drive 1
for that takeout.
.It Pa takeout- Ns Ar YYYYmmdd-HHMMSS Ns Pa .partial/
A takeout in progress, or one that failed; deleted by the next takeout.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Usage errors exit 2.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Find the disk's identifier, erase it as a single APFS volume, and
encrypt it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ diskutil list external
$ diskutil eraseDisk APFS Firesafe-A GPT disk4
$ diskutil apfs encryptVolume /Volumes/Firesafe-A -user disk -passprompt
.Ed
.Pp
Encryption carries on in the background, and the disk can be used
meanwhile.
Then eject it and plug it in again while watching the screen, through
Screen Sharing if need be, and in the password dialog tick
.Dq Remember this password in my keychain .
Then set it up:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ proton-firesafe init /Volumes/Firesafe-A
.Ed
.Pp
Install, set
.Ev MAILTO ,
check that mail works, and start the daily agent:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ make install
$ vi ~/.config/proton-firesafe/config
$ proton-firesafe test-mail
$ make agent
.Ed
.Pp
Run the agent now, rather than waiting for the night, and watch:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ launchctl kickstart gui/$(id -u)/nl.strandkip.proton-firesafe
$ tail -f ~/Library/Logs/proton-firesafe.log
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr launchctl 1 ,
.Xr msmtp 1 ,
.Xr proton-drive 1 ,
.Xr launchd.plist 5 ,
.Xr caffeinate 8 ,
.Xr diskutil 8 ,
.Xr launchd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Joe Abley Aq Mt jabley@strandkip.nl ,
with Claude.
.Sh CAVEATS
Every takeout is a full copy of the account, downloaded afresh; a
takeout of hundreds of gigabytes takes hours.
.Pp
.Xr proton-drive 1
does not export Proton Docs or Sheets.
.Pp
The agent runs in the login session, because
.Xr proton-drive 1
keeps its session, and macOS keeps the disks' passwords, in the login
keychain.
If nobody is logged in, nothing runs, and nothing can say so; a swap
request that is overdue is the sign.
Automatic login keeps a headless Mac logged in after a power cut.
.Pp
The first time the agent writes to an external disk, macOS asks whether
.Xr sh 1
may access files on a removable volume, and waits for an answer; so does
.Xr security 1 ,
reading the mail password from the keychain.
Start the first run by hand while watching the screen, as in
.Sx EXAMPLES ,
and allow both.
.Pp
A takeout is decrypted: anyone with a disk and its password can read
everything on it.
Keep the password somewhere safe, and not only on the Mac, or the disk
in the fire safe will be no use when it is needed.
